          "text": "1-methylcyclohexene reacts with borane, hydrogen peroxide to form trans-2-methylcyclohexanol with 84 percent yield. Alternately, with mercuric acetate and water, then sodium borohydride to form 1-methylcyclohexanol with 90 percent yield."
